  (text "ETHERNET: W5500 (SPI slave, SPI mode 0) + HR911105A RJ45 with integrated 1:1 magnetics and LEDs. Host SPI0 from RP2040: MISO GP16, CS GP17, SCK GP18, MOSI GP19, RST GP20, INT GP21.\nPer W5500 datasheet v1.1.0: 25 MHz crystal (CL=18 pF -> 2x18 pF), 1M across XI/XO, 0R in series with XO (Fig. 3); RSET 12.4k 1% EXRES1->AGND (Fig. 2); TOCAP 4.7 uF; 1V2O 10 nF; VBG floating (NC); RSVD pin 23 to GND.\nAVDD (pins 4/8/11/15/17/21) fed from +3V3 through ferrite bead FB1 with 10 uF + 4x100 nF; VDD (pin 28) 100 nF. PMODE[2:0]=111 (all capable, auto-negotiation). Pins 38-42 RSVD (internal pull-down) NC.\nHR911105A per Hanrun drawing: P1 TD+, P2 TD-, P3 RD+, P6 RD-; P4 (TX centre tap) and P5 (RX centre tap) tied to filtered +3V3A with 100 nF (C40); P7 NC; P8 chassis (1 nF/2 kV inside) and shield to GND.\nLEDs: green (pins 9 anode/10 cathode) = LINK from W5500 LINKLED (active low); yellow (pins 12 anode/11 cathode) = ACT from W5500 ACTLED (active low). 330 R from +3V3. SPDLED/DUPLED unused.\nW5500 has no auto-MDIX: use a straight cable to a switch/router (crossover to a PC without auto-MDIX)."
    (at 20 20 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "c61df25c-4ee5-4fae-9c37-76837b9d9e11")
  )
